IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Employment Relations Act 2000 (New Zealand), dismissal and personal
-- grievances — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Every fact the rule modules read, and nothing else: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2000_24.txt (New Zealand
-- Legislation, version as at 10 July 2026, converted from the PCO XML).
-- Field names are unique across records.

§ `Employment Relations Act 2000 — the nouns`

§§ `Grounds (s 103(1))`

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `(a) unjustifiable dismissal`
    `(b) unjustifiable disadvantage`
    `(c) discrimination`
    `(d) sexual harassment`
    `(da) adverse treatment for family violence`
    `(e) racial harassment`
    `(f) duress over union membership`
    `(g) failure to comply with Part 6A`
    `(h) agreement not in accordance with s 67C, 67D, 67G or 67H`
    `(i) contravention of s 67F or 67G(3)`
    `(j) adverse conduct for a health and safety reason, or coercion`
    `(ja) adverse conduct for a remuneration disclosure reason`
    `(k) retaliation against a whistleblower`

§§ `The employment (ss 67-67B, 67I-67J)`

DECLARE Employment HAS
    `employment began on`                               IS A DATE
    `previously employed by this employer`              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 67A(2): a written trial provision, its period in days (if any).
    `written trial provision for days`                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `notice of termination given on`                    IS A DATE
    -- s 67I(4): remuneration paid in the pay periods within the 364 days
    -- before the pay period of notification, and the days held in them.
    `remuneration in the 364 days`                      IS A NUMBER
    `days held in the 364 days`                         IS A NUMBER
    -- s 113B: the threshold in force (from $200,000).
    `specified remuneration threshold`                  IS A NUMBER
    -- s 67J.
    `agreed in writing that ss 67I and 113A do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The grievance (ss 114, 120)`

DECLARE Grievance HAS
    `ground`                                            IS A Ground
    -- ss 67B(2)(b), 113A(2)(b): whether a (b) grievance relates to the
    -- dismissal.
    `relates to the dismissal`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `action occurred on`                                IS A DATE
    `action came to the employee's notice on`           IS A DATE
    `grievance raised on`                               IS A DATE
    `employer consented to late raising`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `Authority granted leave under s 114(4)`            IS A BOOLEAN
    -- for the Legislation Act 2019 s 55 working day.
    `Matariki Observance Days`                          IS A LIST OF DATE

§§ `Remedies (ss 123B-128)`

DECLARE `Remedy facts` HAS
    `the employee contributed to the situation`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contribution amounts to serious misconduct`    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 124(2): up to 100%.
    `reduction for contribution, in percent`            IS A NUMBER
    `remuneration lost`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `3 months' ordinary time remuneration`              IS A NUMBER
